#    decompression path"); it turns out to be the Ruby zlib GEM.
#  - The remaining four are real product+version matches and stay, but they no
#    longer share a date. Their levers are a long way apart, and the "stagger
#    across weeks" rule exists so a stalled review of one does not carry the
#    other.
#
# The per-entry notes below are rewritten to the verified data. This is a
# renewal in the register's sense — a re-verification, not a date bump.
# ============================================================================

# (ldns CVE-2026-10846 removed 2026-08-04 (#1327): the #1273 pin advance took
#   ldns 1.9.0 -> 1.9.2, which carries the fix; vulnix no longer reports it.)

# libmicrohttpd CVE-2025-59777 and CVE-2025-62689 removed 2026-10-26
# (#1847): the stable pin advance cf5e7650 -> 1f607aa7 ships 1.0.10.
# Both findings are absent from the local scan of the rebuilt closure.

# --- sqlite 3.51.2. Both entries are FTS5 memory-corruption defects fixed in
#     SQLite 3.53.2, reported by VulnCheck (no NIST analyst score). Both are
#     CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H — LOCAL vector requiring
#     USER INTERACTION: the attacker must get a crafted database file opened
#     and an FTS5 MATCH query run against it.
#
#     Provenance: in-closure via the python env and nix's own database.
#     Neither opens a database supplied by an attacker; nix's store DB is
#     local state, and the FTS5 path needs a MATCH query this image never
#     issues against foreign data. Unchanged in substance from the 2026-06-23
#     note, now with the vector verified rather than assumed.
#
#     Lever: FURTHEST of the register. nixpkgs master carries sqlite 3.53.3,
#     past the fix, but nixos-26.05 and staging-26.05 both still ship 3.51.2
#     and no 26.05 backport is open, so advancing the pin changes nothing and
#     nothing is queued that would. 2026-11-11 is the longest window here and
#     sits on its own Wednesday, one past the unbound block. If no backport
#     has appeared by then, the next review renews on this same rationale
#     rather than pretending a lever exists. ---
Expiration: 2026-11-11
# CVE-2026-11822 (7.8) — out-of-bounds read in fts5LeafSeek() plus a heap
#   overflow write in fts5ChunkIterate() via crafted FTS5 page data. Needs a
#   malicious database to be opened and MATCH-queried.
CVE-2026-11822
# CVE-2026-11824 (7.8) — heap overflow in fts5ChunkIterate() from a
#   continuation page declaring szLeaf < 4; same prerequisites as
#   CVE-2026-11822.
CVE-2026-11824

